From: Mr Douvis <douvis@hellenic-culture-ministry.example> (Ministry of Culture, Organising Committee)
To: RAM Media Limited <info@ram-media.example> (RAM Media)
Date: 2006-10-31
Subject: Letter no 79 - terms agreed on 27 October

"After numerous telephone conversations of yesterday and today (30th and 31st of October 2006) we expected from your side confirmation of the issues that were commonly agreed in the meeting concluded on the 27th October ... by which the [Agreement] was further detailed and specified, and which has come into effect as its is described below..."

Clause 3: RAM is relieved of the obligation to provide an international entertainment programme.
Clause 5: the Ministry assumes responsibility for a number of items originally the responsibility of RAM.
Clause 6: "RAM/PMG are contractually obligated to deliver to Athens at their own expense: - at least 6 of the award winning players - award presenters: 4 award presenters (3 places are booked for provision by MoC) as follows: - the 'heros' of the award receivers to give them their trophies, - Other award presenters - celebrities from the football world, - The show presenters (Ruud Gullit and Gabby Logan)..."
Clause 7: total consideration reduced to EUR 2.3 million. Of the two sums of EUR 1.2 million already received by RAM, the first is held by the National Bank. RAM to instruct the National Bank to extend the letter of guarantee to 10th November. On the bank's confirmation EUR 400,000 to be released to RAM, a further EUR 400,000 on 7th November "once it is verified that RAM and PMG have fulfilled all of their above mentioned deliverables and obligations", and the final EUR 300,000 on 17th November.

Failing agreement to these terms by 11:00 on 1st November, the Ministry will terminate the Agreement and hold RAM liable for any amounts paid to RAM and damages.

Douvis
Organising Committee

--
RECONSTRUCTED FROM THE PUBLISHED JUDGMENT. Not an original document.
Source: RAM Media v Ministry of Culture of the Hellenic Republic [2008] EWHC 1835 (QB), paras 157-160, 162-163.
Dated 31 October but faxed 2006-11-01 at 01:27. Clauses 3, 5 and 7 and the last paragraph are the judge's summary. The figure pleaded later was EUR 2.2 million (para 163).
